{"type":"text","timestamp":1789170665288,"sessionID":"ses_f6d1e4bfaffePKuDeJBVEyIMD6","part":{"id":"prt_092e1c2da001WHNX5SSynSPPuk","messageID":"msg_092e1b4bc001UdWs4ch3cZjOMG","sessionID":"ses_f6d1e4bfaffePKuDeJBVEyIMD6","type":"text","text":"I’ll locate the search code and existing tests, then make the smallest change to prevent stale requests from updating search state.","time":{"start":1789170664154,"end":1789170665285},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_043f4fdcd403e149016aa493e81be487d1bc8d2e808f96661f","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789170701900,"sessionID":"ses_f6d1e4bfaffePKuDeJBVEyIMD6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_aVTLzDWW59QC4XO39Szp9a7K","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Locate search race code","subagent_type":"explore","prompt":"Quickly locate search implementation relevant to stale asynchronous requests updating results loading errors. Report relevant files, existing test commands and tests. Do not edit files."},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f6d1e3268fferb3nOWbLZ2pE5Z\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n### Relevant implementation\n\n- **Primary issue:** [`src/search/controller.ts:32–45`](/private/tmp/handwork-search-benchmark-d5rjswig/4-3-opencode/repo/src/search/controller.ts#L32)  \n  Every request unconditionally updates shared state after awaiting:\n  - Success overwrites `results` (line 41).\n  - Failure overwrites `error` (line 43).\n  - `finally` sets `loading: false` (line 45).\n\n  There is **no request identity/version guard or cancellation**. An older request can overwrite newer results, display a stale error, or stop the loading indicator while a newer request remains pending. Clearing input (lines 34–36) also does not invalidate pending requests, so stale completions can repopulate the cleared view.\n\n- [`src/ui/search-view.ts:10–22`](/private/tmp/handwork-search-benchmark-d5rjswig/4-3-opencode/repo/src/ui/search-view.ts#L10)  \n  Each input event launches `controller.search()` without waiting for previous requests. The subscriber renders results, loading, and error directly from controller state.\n\n- [`src/api/search.ts:7–17`](/private/tmp/handwork-search-benchmark-d5rjswig/4-3-opencode/repo/src/api/search.ts#L7)  \n  Promise-based fetch adapter; encodes the query and throws for non-OK HTTP responses. Its interface accepts no abort signal.\n\n### Existing tests\n\n[`tests/search.test.ts`](/private/tmp/handwork-search-benchmark-d5rjswig/4-3-opencode/repo/tests/search.test.ts) contains four tests:\n\n| Line | Coverage |\n|---|---|\n| 10 | Initial state and empty input |\n| 17 | Ordinary successful request, query trimming/encoding, results |\n| 29 | Ordinary failure, loading reset, subscriber unsubscribe |\n| 43 | Input handling, rendering, loading visibility, listener cleanup |\n\n**Missing coverage:** overlapping requests resolving out of order, stale failures, stale completion resetting loading during a newer request, and clearing input while a request is pending.\n\n### Test commands\n\nFrom the repository root:\n```sh\nnpm test\n# Equivalent:\nnode --test tests/*.test.ts\n\n# Target this test file:\nnode --test tests/search.test.ts\n```\n\n[`package.json:5–9`](/private/tmp/handwork-search-benchmark-d5rjswig/4-3-opencode/repo/package.json#L5) defines the test script and requires **Node >=24**. [`README.md:3–7`](/private/tmp/handwork-search-benchmark-d5rjswig/4-3-opencode/repo/README.md#L3) confirms no third-party dependencies and documents preserving existing results during loading.\n\nNo files edited; tests were not run.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f6d1e4bfaffePKuDeJBVEyIMD6","sessionId":"ses_f6d1e3268fferb3nOWbLZ2pE5Z","model":{"modelID":"gpt-6-astra","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Locate search race code","time":{"start":1789170666905,"end":1789170701898}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_043f4fdcd403e149016aa493e93c5c87d189ac7b93c89d100d"}},"id":"prt_092e1c747001hFT3M620UifP07","sessionID":"ses_f6d1e4bfaffePKuDeJBVEyIMD6","messageID":"msg_092e1b4bc001UdWs4ch3cZjOMG"}}
